WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.367
-Looking good, pal.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.634
-Thank you for
coming on the show.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.167
-It's great to be here.
-Yeah, how's life?

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.334
How's everybody?
-They're good.

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:07.400
We keep having kids.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.467
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:09.901
-Congratulations.
You have a new baby girl.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:13.200
-Yes, six months old today.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.968
-Adelaide.
-Adelaide.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.534
-Adelaide.
-Addy.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:18.100
We call her Adelady-ady.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.334
Addy. We're working on it.
It's new.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:21.667
-Six months.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.534
-Does she have a personality
or anything yet?

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.801
-You know, we have
these two older kids

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.467
running around
and she just watches.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:28.834
She's the watcher.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:31.334
And we get the sense
that her whole vibe is

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:34.334
"You've got a lot going on.
I'm going to be chill.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.000
And then maybe when I'm 8 or 9,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.667
all hell's
going to break loose."

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.033
-Yeah, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.667
You brought a photo here.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.267
-This is Ashe and Axel.
They're feeding --

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.701
-This is a great photo
right here of my family.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.000
There you go.
[ Audience aws ]

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.901
First of all, he obviously loves
her if he's willing to

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.167
take off his mask
and reveal his true identity.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.834
[ Laughter ]
-Batman would never do that.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:55.801
-And this is -- Axel always
looks like a small-town mechanic

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:58.734
who's overcharging you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.200
Oh, he just overcharges you.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.734
He's like, "No, you need
a whole new engine."

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.901
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, and look at her eyes.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:06.734
She's like, "Wait, I feel like
there should be a parent here."

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.467
-That's so cute.
-It's really good.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.934
-You also sent another picture
of Axel.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.968
-Yeah.
-You said he has great style.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.801
-He has great style.
And this is an outfit he put on.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:18.901
-Okay.
-I want you to show

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.133
the outfit first.
-Yes.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.334
-Because the minute
he put it on,

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:24.300
I realized he was dressed
like a film character,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.534
a character from a movie
I know that we both love.

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:27.701
-Okay.
-And I want you to see you

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.567
if you can know based on the --

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:31.167
Who do you think
he's dressed like there?

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.067
-Let me see.
-Okay.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:36.334
-He's very cute, first of all.
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.634
-Let me see there.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.100
Yellow pants.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.234
-It's the hair.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.067
Ignore the glasses.
-Yep.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.200
It's the hair.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.834
Is it like a surfer?

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.067
Is it Brad Pitt or something?

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.734
-Alright, show it.
You're going to be mad.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.167
-I am?
-Yeah.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:50.200
-Dang.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:54.367
Oh, my gosh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:57.567
Oh, my God.
-It's full Wooderson, right?

00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:00.267
-Alright, alright, alright.
-Alright, alright, alright.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.701
-He's Matthew McConaughey
in "Dazed and Confused."

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.100
Dude, that's so cute, man.
-Yeah.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.000
-I love when they start
dressing themselves.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.467
-We're doing pretty good. Yeah.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:09.901
-Yeah. Not too shabby.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:13.267
You know, in your stand-up,
"Lobby Baby," which is great,

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:18.634
by the way, you do a bit about
parents of three being more Zen.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:20.033
You feel like there's Zen
with three babies.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.901
-Yeah. And now I realize
it's just that you give up.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.734
I thought they found
some inner peace.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.868
And it's more like, "Well,
there's just too many of them."

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:30.434
-Yeah, that's it.
That's the way you feel?

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:31.968
-Yeah, but the nice thing
about having three is

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:35.167
just the arrogance of telling
people, "Yeah, we have three.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:37.067
Yeah. You have two, Jimmy?

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.701
Oh, my God. Two would be great.

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.601
Yeah, we have three."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.634
"You must have such a full life.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:45.367
We have three."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:48.133
-We got to hang together
for a good little chunk

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:50.000
in Washington, D.C.
-It was the best.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.934
-Because Lorne Michaels received
the Kennedy Center Honor.

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.601
And it was so much fun.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.334
We hung out for like hours.
-It was great.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:03:00.067
It was multi-generations
of "SNL" casts.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.300
And we all were
just hanging out backstage.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.934
And I was saying to people
afterwards --

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:06.767
You would be surprised to know
it, but all we did was

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:09.634
talk about the worst
we'd ever bombed.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:12.367
None of us talked about,
like, doing well anywhere.

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:14.067
-Yeah, oh, yeah.
We're like,

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.901
"What was the worst you ever
bombed on this stage?"

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.601
And everyone had stories.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:20.033
Kate McKinnon was even, like,
in the next dressing room.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.701
She came out just to go like,
"I have a bomb story.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.501
Yeah, I got on stage and just
got crickets. No one laughed."

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:28.267
-Well, because people don't
understand, a lot of times

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:32.033
we have to do things that are
galas or charity events.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.133
-Yes.
-Where people might not want to

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.467
see comedy,
and then when you do it,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.934
they're just confused
and a little bit angry.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:41.300
-Yeah. They're there because
they're supporting the charity.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.033
They're not really there
to see you perform.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.234
-Yeah. And you walk out
and they're immediately like,

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:47.367
"I don't want this."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:48.834
-Do you remember
any painful ones?

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:52.667
-So, it was -- Remember there
was that Madison Square Garden

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.634
benefit for Sandy --
Hurricane Sandy.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.801
-Yes.
-It was like the biggest bands

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.067
in the world.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.400
-And someone reached out
to Lorne and said,

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.634
"We'd love to have
'SNL' do something."

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:04.567
And the best Lorne could come up
with was me as myself

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.334
and Bobby Moynihan
as Drunk Uncle.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.801
Drunk Uncle was an A-plus
"Weekend Update" character.

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:10.267
-Absolutely, yeah.
-Always crushed.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:12.534
-Yes.
-Me and Bobby went out and did

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:15.801
Drunk Uncle, I think, between
The Who and Arcade Fire.

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:18.234
[ Laughter ]
In Madison Square Garden.

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:20.334
And I remember we were standing
backstage and it was starting to

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:22.267
dawn on us
this was a terrible idea.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.334
-Yeah.
-And Chris Rock walked up to us.

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:25.901
And he just looked,
because Bobby was in costume,

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:29.467
and he looked at us and he went,
"You're going to do sketches?

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:30.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:32.000
"You're going to go out there

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.834
and you're going to
do a sketch?"

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.067
It's like,
"Ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:37.801
give it up for The Who!
And now here's a sk--"

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:40.234
It was like
a high school talent show.

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:42.467
-It is so fun.
We kept talking about

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.968
those stories, and everyone
had bits, by the way.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:46.234
Everyone was doing bits.

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:48.133
And like you said,
it was every generation of --

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:51.334
It was from Steve Martin,
Kevin Nealon, Amy Poehler.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:53.467
Everyone was just
on fire and funny.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:57.667
And I remember as we rehearsed
from like 12:00 to maybe 5:00 --

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.234
-It was a long rehearsal, yeah.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.734
-I was leaving
and I was just kind of tired.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.901
I wanted to just to get ready,
get a tux on, get back.

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:07.167
I'm leaving and they go --
I was getting in my car.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:08.868
They have cars to take us
to the hotel.

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:11.167
And I get into my car, they go,
"Jimmy, Kevin Nealon wants to

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:13.534
say hi to you or he wants to say
something to you

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:16.767
and he's in his car."
I go, "Okay."

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:19.033
I go over to the car,
and Kevin's there.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:20.701
I go, "Kevin, do you want me?"

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:23.033
He was just there.
He just rolled his window up

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:28.601
and then took off.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:29.634
That was it.
-That's fantastic.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:30.968
-That's all he wanted.
-That's all.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.767
-Funny, funny bit.
It was so good.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.367
Pal, I'm proud of you.
Look at this one right here.

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:36.367
-There it is.

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:37.667
-"I'm Not Scared,
You're Scared."

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:39.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:40.501
Come on!

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.000
It officially came out today.
-It is.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.367
This is the day
you can buy this book.

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:48.834
-Yes.
What inspired you to write this?

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.534
-It's so funny --
When you have kids,

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.167
they're scared of
a lot of things.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:54.734
And I would say about half of
them, you want to tell them,

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:56.667
"Oh, that's crazy,
don't be scared about that."

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.300
And then the other half,
you, as a parent,

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.901
are so happy they're scared of.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.300
Like traffic.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.467
You don't want to tell your kids
like, "Don't be afraid.

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:04.567
Face your fears!"

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:08.067
-Traffic is something
to be afraid of, yeah.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.567
-So there's this weird thing of
I feel like you have to talk to

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:13.567
your kids in a way -- you can't
just tell -- you have to explain

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:15.834
to them why some fears are okay
and some are not.

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:18.567
And ultimately, kids have to
decide on their own

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:19.767
to stop being afraid
of something.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.334
-That's correct.
-You cannot just yell at them

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:22.767
and tell them
to stop being afraid.

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:25.334
-I love the drawings,
by the way, too.

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.734
-Yeah. Rob Sayegh Jr. -- I want
to make sure I give a shout-out.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:30.167
I did not do the drawings
in my book.

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.300
I did originally and they said,
"This is -- No."

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.868
-"Terrible. Please don't."

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:35.667
-They were like, "We're going to
need the money back."

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:37.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:38.467
-When you read this
to your kids,

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:39.734
do you do different voices?

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:41.234
-They will not let me
do the voices.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.934
-Aww.
-Yeah, no.

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:44.734
It's heartbreaking.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:46.400
It's a very passive-aggressive
way of saying

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.801
they don't care for me
as an actor.

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:50.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:51.601
It happened to me at "SNL" too.

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:53.000
You know, I started as
a cast member.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.701
A lot of people don't know that,
and then, after a few years,

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:56.534
Lorne was like,
"Should you do Update?"

00:06:56.534 --> 00:06:58.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.133 --> 00:06:59.868
"I think your voice,
maybe just your voice."

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:02.267
-"Just do you maybe
behind a desk."

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:05.467
-Yeah. Lorne was like,
"Do we need the legs?"

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:06.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:08.067
-Well, it worked out.

00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:09.534
We're talking more to
Seth Meyers

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:10.801
when we come back, everybody.

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:11.968
Check out his new book.

